  "description": {
   "content": [
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "marks": [
        {
         "attrs": {
          "href": "https://fedora-commons.org/confluence/display/DEV/mail/11503765"
         },
         "type": "link"
        }
       ],
       "text": "https://fedora-commons.org/confluence/display/DEV/mail/11503765",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "> [...] As it stands in 3.1, the ValidationUtility class has a",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> hard-coded rejection of file urls, and the DisseminationService class",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> fetches external content via it's own WebClient (rather than using the",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> ExternalContentManager).  These two quirks prevent (as far as I can",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> tell) an ExternalContentManager module from making non-http content",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> available as datastreams. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "> Would it be reasonable to split ",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "attrs": {
        "url": "https://fedora-repository.atlassian.net/browse/FCREPO-453#icft=FCREPO-453"
       },
       "type": "inlineCard"
      },
      {
       "text": " into 2 issues, so that the",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> changes allowing an ExternalContentManager module to use non-http urls",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "> were separated from the actual implementation of such a module?",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "So, just to make sure, the basic strategy you're thinking of is:",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "First, refactor so that all datastream access (for content stored",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "outside fedora's control) goes consistently through",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "ExternalContentManager.  This includes all runtime access to \"R\" and",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "\"E\" datastreams, as well as \"M\" datastreams when they are ingested by",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "reference.",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
     "content": [
      {
       "text": "Next, add file:// (and potentially other) resolutions to an impl of",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "ExternalContentManager (why not DefaultExternalContentManager?), with",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "adequate administrative control over which dirs on the local machine",
       "type": "text"
      },
      {
       "type": "hardBreak"
      },
      {
       "text": "can be loaded from when the URL happens to be a file:/// one. ",
       "type": "text"
      }
     ],
     "type": "paragraph"
    }
   ],
